    'For residential and inpatient addiction treatment, the gap between the first call and admission is where patients are most often lost. Elixir makes every enquiry a tracked record: calls, web forms and walk-ins land in an inquiry pipeline with call notes, referral source tagging and alerts for missed callbacks, as native Salesforce CRM behavior. Referral source management tracks admissions, conversions and time-to-admit by referring hospital, therapist, court, employer or alumni, and relationships stay in the system when staff leave. Pre-admission screening (substance use history, medical acuity, psychiatric history, withdrawal risk) flows into the clinician’s assessment queue so questions are not re-asked. Real-time 270/271 eligibility checks pull copays, deductibles, prior authorization requirements and behavioral health carve-outs before a bed is promised, and patient financial responsibility is presented during intake. Travel and arrival logistics are logged on the admission record. Admissions coordinators see real-time census and bed availability across facilities. Level-of-care assessment uses configurable templates aligned to the ASAM edition the state requires; a placement recommendation is generated from dimensions 1 to 5, and when clinician judgement differs, the rationale is documented, which helps in utilization review.',
