    'Salesforce Field Service handles scheduling, workforce assignment, dispatch and field operations, but it does not include the electronic visit verification Medicaid requires for personal care and home health services. Elixir complements it: Field Service tells you where the caregiver should be, Elixir EVV verifies the visit, Elixir EHR records the care and Elixir RCM gets the visit ready to bill. Elixir is designed with an EVV aggregator connector framework so visit data can be routed according to payer and state requirements, including open-model submission. Depending on the state and program, integrations may involve platforms such as Sandata, HHAeXchange or other designated EVV systems; connector availability is confirmed for the specific payer and state implementation. Supervisors review flagged visits, approve or reject corrections and preserve the rationale in the audit history, and verification status is used for claim readiness. Organizations using Salesforce Field Service, Health Cloud or Service Cloud can see how Elixir connects EVV to care delivery and billing.',
